# Concept D — Tree Hierarchy

Single wider panel. Projects collapsible; tasks render as children inline. No icon rail.

## Behavior

- Sidebar `w-64`
- Each project = collapsible row w/ chevron
- Expand → tasks listed beneath, indented
- Click project name → select project (kanban view)
- Click task → open task tab
- Multi-select projects can be expanded simultaneously
- Footer same as today (settings, usage, etc.) but laid out horizontally

## Wireframe

```
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ ≡  drag region           │
├──────────────────────────┤
│  🔍 search all tasks     │
├──────────────────────────┤
│  ▾ ⬢ Project A      (3)  │
│      ◉ fix login bug     │
│      ◉ refactor api ⏱   │
│      ◉ ship release      │
│      + new task          │
│                          │
│  ▾ ⬡ Project B      (1)  │
│      ◉ migrate db        │
│      + new task          │
│                          │
│  ▸ ⬡ Project C      (5)  │
│  ▸ ⬡ Project D      (12) │
│                          │
│  + new project           │
├──────────────────────────┤
│ 📊 ⚙ ⌨ 📣              │
└──────────────────────────┘
        w-64
```

## Pros

- Single panel — minimal visual chunking
- Tree natural for hierarchy
- Easy global scanning of all work
- Search at top scopes globally

## Cons

- Loses iconic project rail (brand strong identifier today)
- Long lists scroll a lot
- Reordering projects vs tasks UX must distinguish levels
- Footer collapse from vertical → horizontal = redesign
